    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="1182" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg1048"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/7–945</note>
                <head>No. 705 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Balfour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of Near Eastern and
                        African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Henderson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-09">9th July, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Henderson</hi>, In answer to your enquiry
                    to-day, I send you the following telegraphic record which we received from
                    London of what took place at a plenary session at Yalta on the 10th
                        February.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d705-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="1183" n="1049" xml:id="pg1049"/> You will see that in the earlier part
                    of the record there are one or two points which arrived here corrupt. The
                    general tenour of Stalin’s remarks is, however, clear enough.</p>
                <p>Yours ever</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Balfour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d705-a1.xml" xpointer="d705-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d705-f1" n="1" xml:id="d705-f1-content">
                <p>For the United States record of the proceedings of this meeting, see <ref
                        target="frus1945Malta#pg_897">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Malta and
                        Yalta, 1945, p. 897</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
